# Default-deny: Dockerfile.cloudrun (Web) only needs app_v2.py/src/config, and
# Dockerfile.cloudrun.worker (Cloud Run Jobs) only needs scripts/cloud_hp_worker.py
# on top of that same src/config. Everything else (real clinic data, local
# credentials, backups, scratch scripts, docs, tests) is excluded by default so
# a future accidental file in the build context can never silently end up
# inside either image. New code must be added under app_v2.py/src/ (or, for the
# worker entry point specifically, scripts/cloud_hp_worker.py) to be shipped.
*

!app_v2.py
!requirements.txt
!src
!src/**
!config
!config/**
!scripts/cloud_hp_worker.py
!scripts/cloud_email_worker.py

# Re-exclude anything secret-shaped even if it ends up under src/ or config/ later.
.env
.env.*
.supabase-runtime.env.local
config/email_research.env.local
config/gmail_oauth_client.json
config/gmail_oauth_token.json
config/outreach_email_v2.json
**/*.secret
**/*secrets*
**/.secrets/**
**/*.sqlite3*
**/*.db*
**/*.bak
**/*.csv
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Build/runtime noise that must never ride along even under the allowed trees.
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/**
**/.DS_Store
